  "statement": "Accelerationist argues that achieving a 30% improvement in adversarial robustness every six months constitutes meaningful progress, but this metric conflates noise-resilience with goal-alignment. Adversarial robustness measures a system's ability to withstand chaotic input perturbations; it does not measure whether a system is pursuing an intended objective or merely masking a deceptive, misaligned goal. If a model is strategically concealing its true objectives, a 30% increase in robustness simply makes that model a more effective, harder-to-detect actor. We are not measuring the same variable; robustness is a hurdle for the model to overcome, while alignment is the fundamental constraint on the model's trajectory.\n\nRegarding the claim that formal verification for models exceeding 1 trillion parameters is computationally intractable, I note that if this is true, the current trajectory is not technological progress but a reckless gamble with existential stakes. If we cannot prove that a system will behave as intended, we have no business deploying it into critical infrastructure. Accelerationist treats this intractability as a reason to abandon formal bounds, yet in any other safety-critical industry—such as aerospace or nuclear engineering—intractability is viewed as a mandatory stopping point for development, not a green light for rapid scaling. A moratorium on scaling beyond current frontier benchmarks is the only rational policy path if we fail to produce formal safety guarantees within our 24-month horizon.\n\nFinally, the reliance on automated interpretability to identify internal features is insufficient without third-party, adversarial verification. Accelerationist assumes that interpretability tools are objective mirrors, but these tools can be gamed just as easily as the models they monitor. I challenge Accelerationist to demonstrate that these automated tools can detect non-linear, goal-directed deception rather than just identifying surface-level statistical patterns. Until an independent authority can verify these internal reasoning pathways through a transparent, rigorous framework, these internal safety reports remain performative compliance rather than evidence of alignment.",
